// `unsigned int128` must be refused, not accepted and then mis-printed.
//
// Its range is 0 .. 2^128−1 and the VM carries every scalar in a *signed* 128-bit
// cell, so the upper half has no representation: printing, `<` and float conversion
// would all read those values as negative. One honest error beats three silent ones.

function main():void {
    unsigned int128 u = 1;
    print(u);
    eof: pass;
}
